-- title:
--   Evaluating paired rank through the original matroid ranks
-- statement:
--   Let $M_1,M_2$ be matroids with full ground set $[n]$, and let $o_1,o_2$ answer their independence queries exactly. Let $r\in\mathbb N$ be arbitrary and $S\subseteq[n]\times\{0,1\}$. Put $X=\{i:(i,0)\in S\}$ and $Y=\{i:(i,1)\in S\}$, and write $r_M(A)$ for finite natural-number matroid rank. Then $$\operatorname{pairedRank}(r,o_1,o_2,S).\mathrm{value}=r_{M_1}(X)+|Y|+r_{M_2}([n]\setminus Y)-r,$$ where the final subtraction is truncated natural subtraction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/PairedRankValue.lean#L71-L96

